---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service | Hollywood Time"
  description="Terms and conditions governing the use of the Hollywood Time website, content, syndication feeds, and editorial materials."
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-8">
    <nav class="text-xs text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-black">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">/</span>
      <span class="text-zinc-900 font-bold">Terms of Service</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="border-b-2 border-zinc-950 pb-6 mb-10">
      <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-red-600 block mb-2">Legal Agreement</span>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black font-headline tracking-tight uppercase text-zinc-950">
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm font-mono text-zinc-500 mt-2">
        Effective Date: September 22, 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-zinc-800 font-sans leading-relaxed space-y-8">
      <section class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">1. Agreement to Terms</h2>
        <p>
          By accessing or browsing <strong>hollywoodtime.com</strong> (the "Site"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service and all applicable federal, state, and local laws. If you do not agree with these terms, you are prohibited from using or accessing this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">2. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
        <p>
          All original written articles, criticism, design elements, graphics, logos, and compilations published on Hollywood Time are the proprietary property of Hollywood Time Media LLC, protected under United States and international copyright and trademark laws.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may quote brief excerpts of our articles for journalistic commentary, educational review, or discussion, provided that prominent attribution and an active hyperlink to the original article on <code>hollywoodtime.com</code> are clearly included.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">3. Prohibited Conduct</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li>Use automated scrapers, crawlers, or extraction tools to mirror or republish whole articles without prior express written authorization.</li>
          <li>Engage in any conduct that disrupts, overburdens, or impairs server performance.</li>
          <li>Transmit malicious code, viruses, or harmful scripts.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">4. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
        <p>
          The materials on Hollywood Time are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. While our newsroom strives for impeccable factual accuracy, Hollywood Time makes no express or implied warranties regarding completeness, timeliness, or fitness for a particular purpose.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-4 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-black text-zinc-950">5. Governing Law & Jurisdiction</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms of Service shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of California, United States, without regard to its conflict of law provisions.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
